From c9970c8d660529d1419f5e2f7d0fd2c3724bc940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:43:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tool-search): forward tool_call to directly-listed tools
 instead of refusing [daveey]

The deferred/direct split is read from the live config at dispatch. When
tools.tool_search.defer/eager changes mid-session (shared-config moved
process_manage from defer to eager), every later tool_call to that tool --
the shape the session had been using successfully -- was refused with
"'X' is a directly-listed tool ... The tool was NOT invoked", costing a
round trip each time across 7 sessions.

New tools.tool_search.forward_direct_calls (default False = upstream):
when on, resolve_underlying_call returns a registered direct tool and
scoped_deferrable_names admits every non-bridge tool in the session's
scoped defs, so both scope gates (model_tools bridge + agent executor
unwrap) and the deferred-schema probe still apply.
